 * executor, default db, so acceptance writes its customer evidence inside its own transaction; every existing caller is
 * unchanged). It changes three platform files: the acceptance flag (flags.ts — CUSTOMER_INVITE_ACCEPTANCE_ENABLED, exactly
 * "true", independent of the console flags), its error code (errors.ts) and two keyed-digest purposes for the durable
 * public throttle (config.ts); and the two freeze verifiers (this layer's hooks). It adds nine files: the shared
 * organization bootstrap, the onboarding bridge (the ONE customer module that reaches the platform acceptance core) and
 * its types, the /register/accept page, its client component, server actions and Arabic copy, and the platform
 * acceptance core and its throttle. No schema module, SQL, migration, seed, session, sign-in, business or console file
 * is in either list; /register keeps its page, layout and behaviour.
 *
 * The rule for an approved change is the one C8, ACC-01, the LCP stage and PO-01A…PO-02D2 used: no re-baseline. Each
 * changed file's hunks are recorded here byte for byte, [49510ec's text, PO-02D3's text]; undone, the file is PO-02D2's
 * (49510ec) to the byte (PO02D3_BASE_SHA), so every older pin keeps its strength. Each freeze verifier's PO-02D3 check
 * proves the hunks are each file's only change and the added files are exactly as recorded.
 *
 * Generated from the diff against PO02D3_BASE (each hunk widened with context until it is unique in both files, its
 * 49510ec form nowhere in PO-02D3's); changing a PO-02D3 file means regenerating this record, which is then part of the
 * change under review.
 */
